    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>drawing library</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Matplotlib is used to make sense of data by visualizing it, so it is a data visualization library.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>data visualization library</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Matplotlib is used to visualize data, like the pumpkin pricing data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>lending library</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Matplotlib is used to visualize data, such as the pumpkin pricing data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-3-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Linear Regression uses the following to plot relationships between variables</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a straight line</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Linear regression finds the straight line that best shows the relationship between the inputs and the output.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a circle</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Linear regression works by finding a straight line, not a circle.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a curve</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A curved line is what polynomial regression uses. Linear regression uses a straight line.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-3-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A good Linear Regression model has a ___ Correlation Coefficient</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>low</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Low correlation means the points are scattered everywhere. A good model has a high correlation coefficient.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>high</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A good linear regression model has a high correlation coefficient, with its points close to a neat line.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>flat</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A correlation coefficient is described as high or low. A good model's is high.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
