    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-3-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>If your data is nonlinear, try a ___ type of Regression</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>linear</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Linear regression uses a straight line, and some relationships can't be plotted as a straight line.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>spherical</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. For nonlinear data, polynomial regression fits a curved line instead of a straight one.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>polynomial</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Polynomial regression creates a curved line to better fit nonlinear data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-3-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>These are all types of Regression methods</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Falsestep, Ridge, Lasso and Elasticnet</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The other types to read about are Stepwise, Ridge, Lasso and Elasticnet. Falsestep is not one of them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Stepwise, Ridge, Lasso and Elasticnet</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Stepwise, Ridge, Lasso and Elasticnet are other important types of regression to read about.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Stepwise, Ridge, Lariat and Elasticnet</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The list is Stepwise, Ridge, Lasso and Elasticnet. Lariat is not one of them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-3-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Least-Squares Regression means that all the datapoints surrounding the regression line are:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>squared and then subtracted</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The distances are squared, but then they are added together, not subtracted.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>multiplied</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Each distance is squared, and then all the squared values are added together.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>squared and then added up</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Each distance from the line is squared, then the squares are added up. The best line makes this sum smallest.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
